 "title": "Count the presses of a button",
 "task": "A button on GP15 connects the pin to ground while it is pressed; pin_input turns on the pin's pull-up, so it reads 1 when released. Count the presses (high to low changes) during the first 100 ms after main starts, then return the count. A press can be as short as 1 ms.",
 "lang": "c",
 "starter": "/* count-presses -- practice exercise (MAVILERA, Pico 2)\n * Count the high-to-low changes of GP15 during the first 100 ms, then return the count.\n * Hint: pin_input, pin_read, and time_us to know when 100 ms have passed. Count a change, not a\n * low level: remember the level you read last.\n */\n#include <rp2350.h>\n\nint main(void)\n{\n    pin_input(15);\n    return 0;                           /* replace with your code */\n}\n",
